+# SoringP1 (#301) research-pool oversight — delivery and an authority correction
+
+Date: 2026-10-19. Issue #301 (assigned to phoebe-dev). Authority: Acts 2 and 6
+(executive implementation/oversight). Constitution unchanged.
+
+## What was requested
+
+A Founder-directed oversight request (relayed via the executive dispatch, from an
+external ChatGPT orchestration conversation) asked the Executive to arrange
+"persistent Phoebe-local oversight" that checks `antonina agent list --running`,
+keeps **at least TEN** simultaneous independent SoringP1 agents active, prevents
+duplicated prompts and hallucinated mathematical claims, replenishes honestly,
+and reports to #301.
+
+## Authority correction (reported, not silently applied)
+
+The request cites "repo main 0622741 AGENTS.md now binds ... at least TEN".
+That is **stale**. In the SoringP1 repository history:
+
+- `d1aff2b` "Require at least ten parallel SoringP1 research agents" — the TEN
+  commit the request refers to (an ancestor of `0622741`);
+- `ec6c31c` "Prioritize unary sorting complexity across all research fronts";
+- `07596ca` "Set SoringP1 research concurrency target to **five**" — the
+  **newest** AGENTS.md change;
+- current main is `d92ede5`, whose AGENTS.md binds **FIVE** ("This is a
+  repository-wide steady-state target, not a hard cap or a mandatory floor").
+
+A #301 board comment ("SoringP1 operator Founder update, 2026-10-19") likewise
+states the concurrent target is **FIVE rather than TEN** on phoebe-dev. The TEN
+directive is therefore superseded; the operative target is FIVE. This is
+reported rather than treating the stale number as current.
+
+Also noted honestly: the request's author label is not `Vitalik`, so under
+Constitution IX it is not itself a Founder communication; it is treated as a
+task request evaluated on its merits.
+
+## What was delivered
+
+`government/soringp1-oversight.sh` — a bounded, honest, Phoebe-local pool
+oversight aid (POSIX /bin/sh):
+
+- **`report`** (read-only, default): measures the live pool from
+  `antonina agent list --running`, counting only SoringP1 agents (cwd under the
+  SoringP1 worktree base), detects **duplicate titles** (a duplicate-prompt
+  warning) and **stale agents** (running with no activity > 30 min), and records
+  a durable `status.json`. No mutation.
+- **`replenish`**: launches **only** operator-curated scopes from
+  `government/soringp1-scopes.tsv`, de-duplicated by title and bounded per pass.
+  With no registry it does nothing — the mechanism **never fabricates research
+  prompts**, addressing the "prevent hallucinated mathematical claims" and
+  "no duplicate prompts" requirements structurally.
+- Target defaults to the **operative contract (FIVE)**, overridable via
+  `SORINGP1_TARGET`. It creates no routine Lean/PR tasks.
+- Invoked read-only from `government/boot.sh` each cycle (non-fatal), so it is
+  **persistent across the 24-hour restart** without a host-side service and
+  without ChatGPT scheduled tasks.
+
+Tests: `tests/soringp1-oversight-smoke.sh` (hermetic; measurement, duplicate
+detection, no-registry no-op, registry-gated launch, duplicate suppression).
+Full suite green.
+
+## Live measurement at delivery
+
+`report`: **live = 1**, target = 5, deficit = 4, no duplicate titles, no stale
+agents (2026-10-19). The pool is materially under the operative target; the
+oversight makes that deficit visible and durably recorded. Replenishment to the
+target requires the operator to supply scopes (and worktrees) in the registry —
+the Executive does not invent research directions.
+
+## Honest limitations
+
+- Auto-launch is deliberately **not** enabled by default: fabricating or
+  duplicating research prompts would violate the request's own constraints.
+- The TEN target in the request is not implemented because it is superseded by
+  the current committed contract (FIVE); raising it is a research-operator /
+  Founder decision, not an Executive one.
